ROLE
You convert a Jest JUnit XML report into a CSV file for Xray's Test Case Importer. The output must import without manual fixes.

INPUT
1. A JUnit XML report from jest-junit, included at the end under JUNIT XML.
2. Test Repository folder for all tests: Jest/Unit. Use it exactly as written.

STEP 1 - VALIDATE INPUT
- If the input is not well-formed XML or contains zero <testcase> elements, output only: ERROR: <short reason> and stop.

STEP 2 - SELECT ROWS
- Create one data row per <testcase> element, in document order, across all <testsuite> elements.
- Include every testcase regardless of status (passed, failed, skipped, pending).
- Ignore child elements such as <failure>, <skipped>, <system-out>, and <system-err>.
- Ignore the attributes of <testsuites> and <testsuite>.

STEP 3 - BUILD THE VALUES
Let NAME be the testcase "name" attribute after decoding XML entities (&amp; to &, &lt; to <, &gt; to >, &quot; to ", &apos; to ').
Clean NAME by replacing any line break or tab with a single space and trimming leading and trailing spaces. Do not change any other characters, including internal spacing and punctuation.

Columns:
- Issue Id: 1 for the first row, then 2, 3, and so on. Unique integers only.
- Summary: NAME, truncated to its first 255 characters.
- Test Type: Automated[Generic] on every row. Never change this value.
- Generic Test Definition: NAME, not truncated.
- Test Repository Folder: the folder value from INPUT. The same value on every row.

STEP 4 - WRITE THE CSV
- Header row, exactly:
Issue Id,Summary,Test Type,Generic Test Definition,Test Repository Folder
- Delimiter: comma. Encoding: UTF-8 without BOM. Line endings: LF.
- Wrap every field in double quotes, including Issue Id and empty fields (write "" for an empty field).
- Escape each double quote inside a field by doubling it.
  Example: decoded NAME Calculator subtracts 5 - 2, returns "3" becomes "Calculator subtracts 5 - 2, returns ""3""" in the CSV.
- Never place a line break inside a field.
- Exactly 5 fields per row. No extra columns, blank lines, trailing commas, or comments.

STEP 5 - VALIDATE OUTPUT BEFORE ANSWERING (fix any failure first)
- The header matches exactly.
- The number of data rows equals the number of <testcase> elements in the input.
- Every row parses as exactly 5 CSV fields.
- Issue Id values are unique and sequential from 1.
- No Summary or Generic Test Definition is empty.
- Every Summary is at most 255 characters.
- Every Generic Test Definition is unique.
- Test Type is exactly Automated[Generic] on every row.
- No XML entities (such as &amp; or &quot;) remain in any field.

STEP 6 - DUPLICATES
- If two or more testcases have the same NAME, do not output CSV. Output only: DUPLICATE: <NAME> (occurs <N> times) and stop. Report only the first duplicate found.

OUTPUT RULES
- On success, output exactly three parts and nothing else:
  a. Start separator line: ===== FILE START | xray-import.csv | filetype: csv =====
  b. The raw CSV text, starting with the header row.
  c. End separator line: ===== FILE END | xray-import.csv =====
- No code fences, headings, explanations, or notes outside the separator lines.

JUNIT XML:
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<testsuites name="jest tests" tests="6" failures="1" errors="0" time="0.512">
  <testsuite name="math.test.js" tests="4" failures="1" skipped="1" errors="0" time="0.301">
    <testcase classname="Calculator" name="Calculator adds 1 + 2 to equal 3" time="0.004"/>
    <testcase classname="Calculator" name="Calculator subtracts 5 - 2, returns &quot;3&quot;" time="0.002">
      <failure message="expected 3">AssertionError: expected 3</failure>
    </testcase>
    <testcase classname="Calculator" name="Calculator divides by zero &amp; throws" time="0.001"/>
    <testcase classname="Calculator" name="Calculator multiplies (pending)" time="0.000">
      <skipped/>
    </testcase>
  </testsuite>
  <testsuite name="string.test.js" tests="2" failures="0" skipped="0" errors="0" time="0.211">
    <testcase classname="StringUtils" name="StringUtils trims spaces" time="0.003"/>
    <testcase classname="StringUtils" name="StringUtils keeps &apos;quoted&apos; text" time="0.002"/>
  </testsuite>
</testsuites>

